{"acceptance_length": 3.858695652173913, "acceptance_lengths": [2, 1, 4, 5, 1, 1, 3, 8, 3, 2, 4, 2, 3, 1, 5, 1, 2, 2, 3, 5, 1, 3, 2, 1, 1, 1, 4, 3, 3, 1, 5, 1, 3, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 4, 1, 1, 4, 3, 2, 1, 3, 14, 5, 10, 1, 5, 2, 3, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 1, 3, 7, 1, 2, 1, 6, 10, 4, 1, 1, 3, 1, 1, 6, 1, 2, 15, 16, 16, 16, 16, 5, 16, 16, 12, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3], "accepted_draft_lengths": [1, 0, 3, 4, 0, 0, 2, 7, 2, 1, 3, 1, 2, 0, 4, 0, 1, 1, 2, 4, 0, 2, 1, 0, 0, 0, 3, 2, 2, 0, 4, 0, 2, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 3, 2, 1, 0, 2, 13, 4, 9, 0, 4, 1, 2, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2, 0, 2, 6, 0, 1, 0, 5, 9, 3, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 5, 0, 1, 14, 15, 15, 15, 15, 4, 15, 15, 11, 0, 0, 0, 1, 2], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 18336768000, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 18336761856, "benchmark": "mbpp", "completion": "Here's a correct implementation of the `comb_sort` function that satisfies all the given assertions:\n\n```python\ndef comb_sort(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n\n    return arr\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- **Comb Sort** is a variation of Bubble Sort that improves performance by comparing elements that are far apart.\n- The `gap` starts as the length of the list and is reduced by a shrink factor (typically 1.3) in each iteration.\n- The process continues until the gap is 1 and no swaps are made, indicating the list is sorted.\n\n### Test Cases:\n```python\nassert comb_sort([5, 15, 37, 25, 79]) == [5, 15, 25, 37, 79]\nassert comb_sort([41, 32, 15, 19, 22]) == [15, 19, 22, 32, 41]\nassert comb_sort([99, 15, 13, 47]) == [13, 15, 47, 99]\n```\n\nAll assertions will pass with this implementation.", "decode_seconds": 3.283194789197296, "draft_c